# Refresh the tokens. Start the API with Aspire first, then send "Create an account" once.
@host = http://localhost:5279

### Create an account → 201. The requests below use its refresh token.
# @name createAccount
POST {{host}}/api/v1/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "user-{{$guid}}@example.com",
  "password": "password",
  "timeZone": "Europe/Zagreb"
}

### Refresh → 200 with new tokens. Send it twice: the second time is 401, because a refresh token works once.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/sessions/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{createAccount.response.body.$.refreshToken}}"
}

### Unknown refresh token → 401 user.invalid_refresh_token.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/sessions/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "not-a-real-token"
}
